Z||000000||sqoach||03-22-2001||05:02 PM||||hey everyone. i just got my new fan switch and 180^ thermostat from rodney today. the stat seems to work great. however, when the temp reached up to 205 (or 195, whatever it's suppost to be), the fan didn't kick in. i even let it get up to 220, still nothing happened. my fan does work though. right when i hit the a/c button, the fan turns on. i don't get it. any ideas?<P>BTW, i think i might have found where air could be getting in the system. everytime i run my car, all the hoses expand (of course). when my car was warmed up, i was checking around the radiator cap for leaks when i noticed a tiny little bit of coolant on the little hose that connects the radiator to the overflow tank. that little collar that holds the hose to the radiator was not holding very good. the teeth are worn and as the hose expanded, the collar would get loose and allow air in there. i hope that's the case anyway.<P>thanks for reading. i hope someone can maybe tell me why the new switch is not working.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||03-22-2001||05:43 PM||||what temp is Rodneys switch supposed to open? I think the stock one dont turn on till 230*. I put a 175* switch in mine. Just put a small hose clamp where the overflow connects. did you 'burp' the coolant at the thermostat cap?<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||03-22-2001||05:52 PM||||on his website, it says it's suppose to turn on at 205, but on the little booklet thingy i got with the package today, it says 195. either way, it should have come on by at least 205.<P>i got another one of those little clamps from my parts car. the teeth on it are not worn at all and it is holding good. the other one was just not holding when the hose heated up and expanded. and i made sure i did a good job of burping the system. there were no temp spikes or anything while i had it running.<p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 03-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||03-22-2001||06:00 PM||||What are you measuring the temp with? If it is the dash gauge that is only a approximate gauge.  Is not very accurate. It certainly is not capable of being accurate within 5 degrees. ||||reg||1
