Z||000008||sqoach||03-22-2001||08:29 PM||||i'm gonna check my relay connections. i found the same color wire that the fan switch connector had (green with a white stripe) that connects to the relay. maybe it's not a good connection. after that, i'm completely clueless as to why this wouldn't work.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Wolfhound||03-22-2001||09:09 PM||||Code 34 is MAP sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000010||sqoach||03-22-2001||09:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Wolfhound:<BR><B>Code 34 is MAP sensor.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ok, so what does that mean? what do i need to do with the MAP sensor? i had the car running for a while and the check engine light never came on.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroJoe||03-22-2001||09:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B> ok, so what does that mean? what do i need to do with the MAP sensor? i had the car running for a while and the check engine light never came on.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I dont think you need to worry about the MAP sensor, just check the hoses for it and make sure it is connected to the air cleaner well.<P>Otherwise, I would go for your relay connections.  You know the relay fires, because the fan comes on when you kick in the AC.  But, the wire that connects your new fan switch to the relay may be bad, so the switch may be making the connection like it is supposed to, but it's not firing the relay because the connection at the relay is bad.<P><P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||sqoach||03-22-2001||10:12 PM||||i think the reason that code showed up is because i did have the hoses disconnected for a little bit to get to the fan switch. and i turned the car on a couple times. the code's not showing now after i disconnected, then reconnected the battery.<P>anyway, joe, should i try another relay? that one in there is not even a year old. i was really messing with the relay and the connections when the temp got high enough, tried wiggling it around. no luck.||||reg||1
Z||000013||sqoach||03-22-2001||10:54 PM||||ok i just tried something else. i grouned the fan switch wire and i heard a click up front (fan relay?) and the fan kicked on. does that mean the (new) fan switch is bad????? i put a bunch of that teflon tape around it before i installed it. does the switch need to be touching the block as a ground?? doesn't really make sense, but either that, or the switch is bad. i let my car get plenty hot enough. let it idle for about 20 minutes. the temp gauge was rising steadily. maybe i didn't screw the fan switch in enough? i got it really tight though. just couldn't go any further cuz of that teflon tape.||||reg||1
