Z||000019||sqoach||03-23-2001||08:33 PM||||but i let my temp gauge get all the way up to near 240 last time i tried this. fan switch should come on around 200. the gauge can't be off that much.<P>there's only 3 explanations here:<BR>1-fan switch is bad<BR>2-my temp gauge is not giving an accurate reading at all<BR>3-the coolant around the fan switch sensor is not as hot as the coolant around the gauge sensor. (kinda off the wall, cuz they're pretty close to each other)<P>here's a question for anyone: how long does it take for your fan to kick on while you car is sitting at idle? (temperature outside was around 60^F)||||reg||1
